      <p>You can uninstall OpenShift Virtualization by using the web console or the command-line interface (CLI) to delete OpenShift Virtualization workloads, the Operator, and its resources.</p>
      <p>To uninstall OpenShift Virtualization, perform the following tasks:</p>
      <ol>
      <li>Delete the <code>HyperConverged</code> CR.</li>
      <li>Delete the OpenShift Virtualization Operator.</li>
      <li>Delete the <code>openshift-cnv</code> namespace.</li>
      <li>Delete the OpenShift Virtualization custom resource definitions (CRDs).</li>
      </ol>
      <h2 id="prerequisites_uninstalling-virt" class="group scroll-mt-20">Prerequisites<a href="#prerequisites_uninstalling-virt" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <ul><li>Delete all virtual machine instances. You cannot uninstall OpenShift Virtualization while its workloads remain on the cluster.</li></ul>
